Ladybird’s CSS.registerProperty() accepts light-dark() and system
colors in a <color> initial value, as the other engines do. Blink’s
CSSValue::IsComputationallyIndependent() returns true for identifiers
and for a CSSLightDarkValuePair. Gecko parses an initial value with
DISALLOW_COMPUTATIONALLY_DEPENDENT, which only font- and container-
relative length units check. And WebKit’s ComputedStyleDependencies::
isComputationallyIndependent() looks only at dependencies on other
properties, containers and anchors, which colors don’t add.
